(e) enter the final decision of the First Division Officer
perusing the file;
(f) in the case where an inquest has been instituted, he
shall enter in the Register—
(i) the date of hearing;
(ii) any postponement;
(iii) the Coroner’s decision (in red ink);
(iv) in addition, if the Coroner’s verdict
discloses a crime, he shall enter the crime
in the relevant register and cross reference
it with the Occurrence Register.
6. (1) The First Division officer, on receipt of the file from the
Second Division Officer-in-charge of the Station, if after perusal,
he is satisfied that there is no criminal liability, recklessness or
foul play, he shall return the file to the Second Division Officer-in-
charge of the Station with instructions to “mark off” the
occurrence.
(2) However, in the case of unnatural death where it is
necessary to have an inquest conducted, he shall cause three (3)
copies of the file to be made. Statements are to be typewritten and
original documents photocopied.
